AltoConvexCreditLineMarket::claimInterest()
├── when market is paused
│   └── it should revert with IsPaused for PAUSE_TYPE
├── when fee recipient is zero address
│   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketZeroAddress before the amount check
├── when caller is neither owner nor fee recipient
│   ├── it should allow partial claims and mint only to the configured fee and reward recipients
│   ├── it should allow claiming all remaining fees with zero amount
│   └── it should return zero without minting or emitting when no fees are available
├── when any caller requests more than claimableFeesAssets
│   ├── when interest fits in uint128
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput without minting or changing accounting
│   └── when interest exceeds uint128 max
│       └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput without minting or changing accounting
├── given caller is owner
│   ├── when interest is zero
│   │   ├── it should claim all available fees
│   │   └── it should return zero without minting or emitting when no fees are available
│   └── when interest is nonzero and at most claimable fees
│       ├── when interest is less than claimable fees
│       │   └── it should perform a partial claim and preserve the remainder
│       └── when interest equals claimable fees
│           └── it should claim the full balance and set claimableFeesAssets to zero
├── given caller is fee recipient
│   ├── when interest is zero
│   │   ├── it should claim all available fees
│   │   └── it should return zero without minting or emitting when no fees are available
│   └── when interest is nonzero and at most claimable fees
│       ├── when interest is less than claimable fees
│       │   └── it should perform a partial claim and preserve the remainder
│       └── when interest equals claimable fees
│           └── it should claim the full balance and set claimableFeesAssets to zero
├── given a successful claim
│   ├── it should decrease claimableFeesAssets by the claimed amount
│   ├── it should mint the configured treasury share to rewardRecipient and the remainder to feeRecipient
│   ├── it should mint exactly the claimed amount across both recipients
│   ├── it should not change debt supply collateral or share accounting
│   ├── it should not accrue interest or call the IRM oracle or Convex contracts
│   ├── it should split opening fees and accrued interest from the same balance
│   ├── it should remain claimable after governance foreclosure leaves recorded fees outstanding
│   ├── it should not reduce badDebtAssets when fees from foreclosed debt are claimed
│   ├── it should emit InterestClaimed for each nonzero share with its recipient and actual amount
│   └── it should return the total claimed across both recipients
├── given the treasury share is zero
│   └── it should mint and emit only for feeRecipient
├── given the full claim is allocated to treasury
│   └── it should mint and emit only for rewardRecipient
├── when calculating the treasury share produces a fractional token unit
│   ├── it should round the treasury share up and leave the remainder to feeRecipient
│   └── when rounding leaves no fee recipient share
│       └── it should mint and emit only for rewardRecipient without calling a zero mint
├── given both recipients are the same address
│   └── it should mint exactly the total claim and emit each nonzero share
└── when either recipient mint fails
    └── it should roll back both balances total supply the minter bucket and claimable fees
